From: Mobile NixOS
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qcom_scm: Enable qseecom for OnePlus 6 (enchilada)

The QSEECOM driver has an allowlist of "tested" machines. The OnePlus 6
(SDM845) has a working TEE but is not in the list, causing:
  "qseecom: untested machine, skipping"

Add it to the allowlist so fingerprint/TEE apps can work.
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index abc123..def456 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2291,6 +2291,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
+	{ .compatible = "oneplus,enchilada" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,inspiron-14-plus-7441" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,latitude-7455" },
 	{ .compatible = "dell,xps13-9345" },
